  "id": "Compound::DB00869 - Gene::762",
  "verbalization": "Dorzolamide is likely to interact with Ca4 through a series of molecular and biochemical pathways. The evidence suggests that Dorzolamide binds to Ca5a, Ca12, or Ca6, all of which participate in the reversible hydration of carbon dioxide. This process is then participated by Ca4, indicating a potential functional relationship between these entities. The binding of Dorzolamide to any of these calcium-related proteins may influence the hydration process, thereby affecting the availability or activity of Ca4. The consistent involvement of Ca4 in the hydration pathway across different binding sites implies that Dorzolamide may modulate the activity of Ca4 through a shared biochemical mechanism, possibly by altering the structural or functional state of the calcium ions involved. This integrated pathway highlights the role of calcium in a critical metabolic process, suggesting that Dorzolamide could exert its effects through a mechanism that involves the regulation of calcium-dependent enzymatic activities.",
